\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Physical parameter values for the results presented within this paper, including value ranges for nondimensional numbers for the chosen parameters. The values of water were used throughout the main body of the text in section \ref {sect:Results}, with the switch to silicone oil used in the extension to Faraday pilot-waves in section \ref {sect:Conclusion}. Silicone oil is used experimentally and, due to the increased viscosity and decreased surface tension, also results in less stringent numerical timestepping. }}{28}{table.caption.14}\protected@file@percent }
